contract:
The shared HTTP + SSE contract, verbatim from packages/chess-core/src/api.ts (exported from @chess-tutor/chess-core; coordinator-owned, do not edit; report any gap in contract_gaps):

import type { Color } from "./types.ts";

/**
 * HTTP + SSE contract between apps/server and apps/web (#6: FR-1, FR-4, FR-5, IR-5).
 * Coordinator-owned: change it only on main, before the spokes that depend on it.
 *
 * Endpoints (JSON bodies, all under /api; errors are `ApiError` with the status shown):
 *   POST /api/games                 NewGameRequest -> 201 GameView
 *        If the player is Black, botThinking is true and the bot's first move arrives over SSE.
 *        Creating a game while another is still "playing" marks the old one "abandoned" (and saves it).
 *   GET  /api/games/:id             -> 200 GameView | 404
 *   POST /api/games/:id/moves       PlayMoveRequest -> 200 GameView with the player's move applied
 *        (botThinking true unless the game just ended). 400 illegal or malformed move;
 *        409 not the player's turn, bot thinking, or game not "playing"; 404 unknown game.
 *   POST /api/games/:id/takeback    -> 200 GameView, back at the player's previous turn
 *        (removes the bot's reply, if any, and the player's last move). 409 while the bot is
 *        thinking, when the game is not "playing", or when the player has no move to undo.
 *   POST /api/games/:id/resign      -> 200 GameView, status "finished", endReason "resigned".
 *   GET  /api/games/:id/events      -> text/event-stream. Each message is `event: <GameEvent.type>`
 *        plus `data: <GameEvent as JSON>`. The first message on every connection is "state".
 *
 * Finished and abandoned games are saved as PGN (FR-5). The bot replies within 2 s (NFR-3).
 */

export type GameStatus = "playing" | "finished" | "abandoned";
export type GameResult = "1-0" | "0-1" | "1/2-1/2" | "*";
export type GameEndReason =
  | "checkmate"
  | "stalemate"
  | "threefold_repetition"
  | "insufficient_material"
  | "fifty_moves"
  | "resigned"
  | "abandoned";

export interface MoveView {
  uci: string;
  san: string;
  by: "player" | "bot";
}

export interface GameView {
  id: string;
  playerColor: Color;
  /** FEN of the current position. */
  fen: string;
  /** Every move from the start position, in order. */
  moves: MoveView[];
  status: GameStatus;
  /** "*" while playing or when abandoned. */
  result: GameResult;
  endReason: GameEndReason | null;
  /** True while the server is choosing the bot's reply; the board accepts no player move then. */
  botThinking: boolean;
}

export interface NewGameRequest {
  playerColor: Color;
}

export interface PlayMoveRequest {
  /** UCI, e.g. "e2e4", "e7e8q"; castling as king two squares ("e1g1"). */
  uci: string;
}

export type GameEvent =
  | { type: "state"; game: GameView }
  | { type: "bot_move"; move: MoveView; game: GameView }
  | { type: "game_over"; game: GameView }
  | { type: "error"; message: string };

export interface ApiError {
  error: string;
}

Color is "w" | "b" (packages/chess-core/src/types.ts).

Ports: apps/server listens on PORT (default 3001, constant DEFAULT_PORT in apps/server/src/main.ts placeholder). apps/web/vite.config.ts serves on 5173 and proxies /api to http://localhost:${SERVER_PORT ?? 3001}. Root `pnpm dev` runs `pnpm --parallel --filter "./apps/*" dev`.

E2E arrangement (both spokes must match it): Playwright runs from apps/web. Its webServer starts the real server with env PORT=3101, DB_PATH=:memory:, LICHESS_TOKEN="" (unset/empty => the server's bot plays engine-only, no network), via `pnpm --filter @chess-tutor/server start`, and vite with SERVER_PORT=3101 on port 5174 (--strictPort). The server must honour PORT, DB_PATH and an empty LICHESS_TOKEN exactly like that.

Building blocks available (already on main, import from workspace packages; read their source for details):
- @chess-tutor/chess-core: createSparringBot({ explorer: BotExplorer, engine: BotEngine, config: BotConfig, random? }) -> { chooseMove(fen): Promise<BotMove> }, BotMove = { uci, san, source: "explorer"|"engine", explorer?, fallbackReason? }. BotExplorer = { lookup(fen, { ratings: number[], speeds: string[] }): Promise<{ moves: {uci,san,games}[], totalGames: number, unavailable?: string }> }. BotEngine = { bestMove(fen, opts?: { elo?: number }): Promise<string> }. parseRepertoirePgn(text, color) -> RepertoireLineInput[] (throws on bad text); buildRepertoire(lines) -> Repertoire. sanOf(fen, uci).
- @chess-tutor/engine: createEngineFromEnv(opts?: { threads?, hashMb? }) -> StockfishEngine (WASM by default, native via STOCKFISH_PATH), with bestMove(fen, {elo}) and quit(). One search at a time per process, queued.
- @chess-tutor/explorer: createExplorerClient({ token, cache }) throws ExplorerConfigError on an empty token; createSqliteExplorerCache(path) with close(). Lookups time out at 1500 ms by default.
- config/tutor.json (repo root): { "engine": { "flavor": "full", "threads": 4, "depth": 18, "movetimeCapMs": 1000, "multiPv": 3 }, "bot": { "explorerRatings": [1200, 1400], "explorerSpeeds": ["blitz", "rapid"], "minGames": 20, "outOfBookElo": 1400 }, ... }. bot block is a BotConfig. Reference wiring: packages/chess-core/scripts/demo-bot.ts.
- repertoire/london.pgn (color "w") and repertoire/kid.pgn (color "b"), multi-game PGN with [Line "..."] headers.
- apps/server/package.json already has deps chess-core, engine, explorer, chess.js, fastify ^5.12.8, and scripts dev/start running node --experimental-strip-types --disable-warning=ExperimentalWarning --env-file-if-exists=../../.env src/main.ts (node:sqlite's ExperimentalWarning is therefore already silenced; keep it that way).
- Node 22 with type stripping: relative .ts imports carry their extension. Vitest picks up apps/server/test/**/*.test.ts from the root config.

Decisions made by the coordinator:
- No LICHESS_TOKEN (empty or unset): log one clear warning at startup and give the bot a stub explorer whose lookup returns { moves: [], totalGames: 0, unavailable: "no_token" }, so it plays engine-only (~outOfBookElo). With a token, use the real client and a SQLite explorer cache in the same database file.
- DB_PATH env, default <repo root>/data/chess-tutor.sqlite (create the directory; *.sqlite is gitignored). ":memory:" must work. One games table at least (id, player_color, status, result, end_reason, pgn, created_at, updated_at); design it so tutor comments can be added later (FR-5 says "with the tutor's comments", which arrive with #7: leave room, don't implement).
- A game is saved when it becomes finished (checkmate, stalemate, draw rules, resign) or abandoned (a new game was created while it was playing, or the server shut down with it playing: handle SIGINT/SIGTERM, then quit the engine and close the DB).
- PGN: standard Seven Tag Roster; White/Black are "Player" and "Sparring bot" by playerColor; Result header matches GameView.result ("*" for abandoned) plus a Termination or comment giving endReason.
- Structure for testability: a createApp/buildServer factory taking injected dependencies (bot, store, clock/id generator as needed) separate from main.ts, which wires the real engine/explorer/config/repertoire. Tests use a fake bot (deterministic, optionally delayed) and fastify.inject; at least one SSE test over a real socket (listen on port 0).
- A takeback while the bot is thinking is 409 (contract). If the bot's search finishes for a game that was since abandoned or changed, discard the move.
- If the bot throws, push an SSE "error" event and leave the game playing with botThinking false so the UI isn't stuck; log it.
- Log the bot's latency per move (ms, source) at info level; a test with the real WASM engine and the stub explorer asserts a bot reply in under 2000 ms (the engine integration test in packages/engine already runs in about 1 s, so this is affordable).

